  "clause": "reached_holds (spline legs)",
  "case": 0,
  "step": 2,
  "note": "A spline leg from the stopping point (0, 0, -300) to (0, 0, -10), leaving towards (0, 1e-6, -10): its origin velocity is 0 and its destination velocity tiny but not zero, so it is a fast waypoint. Tick 0 starts it (the initialization zeroes the desired velocity, so the spline time stays 0). Tick 1 (dt 1e-4, desired velocity 1e-6 m/s) advances the spline time to about 3e-7 (the zero-velocity branch of SplineCurve::calc_dt_speed_max, spline_dt = sqrt(2 d / |a|)). Tick 2: the position stage reports a desired velocity of 30 m/s; the spline velocity at that time is about 6e-4, so spline_dt = d / |v| is over 100 and SplineCurve::advance_target_along_track sets the time to 1 and reached; the target of that tick is still computed at the old time (the origin), 290 m from the destination, and AC_WPNav reports the leg finished (s_finished, fast waypoint). In ArduCopter the desired velocity is the target velocity of the previous tick, so the jump needs a position stage that does not follow the target; reached_holds is stated for S-curve legs only. Inputs added later (12: the `_seq` call-order fields and signals) are 0/false: fixed order, the steps are unchanged.",
